  "method_notes": [
    "Roache's asymptotic-range ratio GCI_medium/(r^p GCI_fine) is an algebraic identity equal to f_fine/f_medium for a single three-grid triplet (same Fs, same triplet), so on a *three-density* study it is almost always ~1 and does not test p at all: here the ratios are 0.91-0.99 (inside any +-10 % band) while every observed order but one is negative.  G6 is therefore gated on monotone AND p > 0; otherwise an anti-convergent sequence would be 'admitted' by an identity.  Testing the asymptotic range needs a fourth level and a comparison of successive triplets (see benchmarks/kp505_gci_ladder.py, triplet disagreement ~30x)."
  ],
